  "provenance_note": "Measured from photographs of fifteen prepared standards of known concentration, supplied by the laboratory on 13 November 2026. These replace colours that were interpolated from an illustration: the concentration of every level is now backed by a prepared standard, which is what the chart was missing. It is still marked ILLUSTRATIVE, and the reason is the photography, not the chemistry. The fifteen shots were taken at different times, by different hands, under different light, with no grey card or colour reference in any frame. Each was white balanced against the sheet of paper behind the tube, which is the only reference available and is a partial correction, not a calibration. The consequence is measurable and is recorded per level in separation_note: four steps are non-monotonic, where a higher concentration photographed LIGHTER than the one below it, and three adjacent pairs sit within dE2000 5 of each other, which is close to indistinguishable. Both are consistent with lighting variation between shots rather than with the dilution series. To make this VALIDATED: re-photograph all sixteen standards in one session, one camera, fixed lighting, with a grey card in every frame, and include 450 ppm.",
